	'nuances' => array(
		'EMIT ș AND ț WITH THE COMMA BELOW (U+0219, U+021B), NEVER THE CEDILLA ş/ţ — the clearest machine-translation tell in Romanian, still shipping live inside otherwise correct sentences („diferenţialelor” for „diferențialelor”). Write â inside words and î at word edges, and never drop a diacritic („arbori cotiți”, not „cotiti”).',
		'PUNCTUATE TO ROMANIAN STANDARD AND HOLD ONE CONVENTION PER DOCUMENT: decimal comma („0,1 g·mm”), thousands period („10.000”), currency after the number, 24-hour time, and one date format sitewide — DD.MM.YYYY. Never mix a numeric date with a spelled-out month in one component: the live resource hub shows „11.08.2026” in one rail and „11 august 2026” in the rail beside it. Quotations open „ and close ” — check BOTH ends, never a straight quote or an English “ ”.',
		'INSERT THE MANDATORY PARTITIVE „de” AFTER ANY NUMERAL ABOVE 19 („500 de companii”, „30 de minute”). Counter and badge labels receive a JS-injected numeral immediately before them, so the label string itself must begin with „de”: „de ani de inovație”. Never translate such a label as if it stood alone.',
